{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3be14dea938aba090375f52f58ba5f9c7217ec0acf8513aaa08120537a81da3e","digest":{"component_or_area":"dependency management / Bedrock SDK","key_entities":["botocore>=1.43.0","boto3>=1.43.0","pyproject.toml","uv.lock","pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]","inspect-ai","aioboto3","aiobotocore","[tool.uv] conflicts block","outputConfig"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock sdk floor","botocore version","boto3 version","structured output","outputconfig","dependency resolution","version lock"],"propositions":["Bedrock Converse outputConfig (native structured output) is rejected client-side by botocore 1.40.61 with ParamValidationError before network calls.","The wire feature requires botocore >= 1.43.0 and matching boto3 >= 1.43.0.","Current dependency constraints lock botocore at 1.40.61 due to a diamond: [eval] -> inspect-ai -> aioboto3 -> aiobotocore caps boto3 < 1.40.62, conflicting with pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock] need for newer.","Explicit floor botocore >= 1.43.0 and boto3 >= 1.43.0 must be added to pyproject.toml alongside pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock] with uv.lock regenerated.","The existing [tool.uv] conflicts block should absorb the floor without change, forking eval and bedrock resolution to keep both installable."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787316200846160001,"uuid":"5a8c4ebc-936b-44aa-b98a-1e86f5e6f3ad"}